{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","title":"The Cartographer's Algorithm","logline":"When cartographer Veya’s calculations predict the skybridges will fail, she must convince the toll-master Kael to release his grip on the last stable routes before the Drift Cartel suppresses her proof and the drifting isles are stranded.","theme":"Truth protects people best when it is shared, not controlled.","acts":[{"id":"act_setup","title":"A Pattern in the Drift","purpose":"setup","scenes":[{"id":"scn_fading_lines","title":"The Fading Lines","summary":"At Silverspine Academy, Veya compares fading bridge charts with wind-current observations and finds a pattern suggesting the isles are drifting apart. Certain she has found the answer, she dismisses a conflicting measurement as an error.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Use the old charts and her wind-sight to establish whether bridge movement follows a predictable pattern.","conflict":"Veya's stubbornness leads her to discard evidence that challenges her first calculation.","outcome":"Her incomplete model predicts a dangerous shift on a key route, but she knows she needs better observations before she can prove it.","depends_on":[]},{"id":"scn_cartel_claim","title":"A Claim on the Routes","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael moves to secure the remaining stable routes for the Cartel, arguing that strict tolls are the only way to manage scarce crossings. He learns that Veya is preparing new charts and resolves to take them before they undermine his plan.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael"],"goal":"Seize control of the last stable skybridge routes before they collapse.","conflict":"Kael's belief that trade must be regulated at any cost turns a warning about failing bridges into another opportunity to consolidate control.","outcome":"Kael orders that Veya's charts be obtained, putting the Cartel in direct opposition to her investigation.","depends_on":["scn_fading_lines"]},{"id":"scn_grain_routes","title":"Paths Beneath the Mills","summary":"Veya reaches The Hollow seeking practical observations of how the routes have shifted. Maris shows her concealed paths among the windmills and granaries, but insists that any help must also protect the isle from the Cartel's grain levy.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Find reliable route observations that can test Veya's model while helping Maris protect The Hollow's grain.","conflict":"Maris distrusts Veya's motives, while Veya is reluctant to share her theory before she can prove it.","outcome":"They agree to exchange Veya's wind-current knowledge for Maris's access to hidden route records, giving the investigation new evidence.","depends_on":["scn_fading_lines"]}]},{"id":"act_rising_action","title":"Evidence Under Pressure","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_hidden_records","title":"The Hollow's Records","summary":"Using Maris's knowledge of the service corridors, the pair compare grain-delivery records with Veya's chart. The records expose a mismatch Veya's first model cannot explain; after resisting Maris's challenge, Veya revises her assumptions.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Test Veya's prediction against independent records of travel between the isles.","conflict":"The evidence contradicts Veya's preferred calculation, and Maris will not risk her people on a theory Veya refuses to question.","outcome":"Veya corrects the model and identifies a route shift that can be checked at Emberroost.","depends_on":["scn_grain_routes"]},{"id":"scn_emberroost_test","title":"Strain in the Cloudstone","summary":"At Emberroost, Veya checks her revised prediction against the condition of the braided skybridge cables. Kael arrives to press his claim on the route and demands the charts, but Veya refuses to hand over an unverified model.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Verify the predicted shift against the bridge's physical condition before publishing the chart.","conflict":"Kael's demand for control clashes with Veya's need to verify the evidence; her fear of becoming like Cartel leaders makes her guard the work too closely.","outcome":"The cable strain confirms a near-term shift, but Veya withholds the full chart, leaving Kael free to continue consolidating the routes.","depends_on":["scn_hidden_records","scn_cartel_claim"]},{"id":"scn_levy_bargain","title":"The Price of Grain","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael offers to ease the grain levy if Maris reveals her supply paths. He prices the arrangement as if its value were only a matter of trade, and Maris refuses; Veya instead shows him enough evidence to warn that his chosen route is at risk.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Convince Kael to stop using the grain levy to force control of the routes and to take the drift prediction seriously.","conflict":"Kael equates price with worth and dismisses the human cost of the levy, while Maris refuses to trust a bargain that exposes her people.","outcome":"Kael rejects the warning but sees that Veya's evidence may threaten his monopoly, and Maris keeps her routes secret.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_test"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Route Gives Way","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_claim_stable_route","title":"The Last Stable Crossing","summary":"Kael moves to seize the last stable route at Mistral Docks, pursuing his goal even as Veya warns that the route will shift. Maris uses her knowledge of hidden paths to bring the grain-route records that corroborate Veya's model.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Kael aims to secure the crossing; Veya and Maris aim to put the prediction and its supporting evidence before those who depend on it.","conflict":"Kael's need for control and Veya's instinct to keep her work close leave little time to act on the approaching shift.","outcome":"Maris's records strengthen the prediction, and Veya chooses to share the complete chart, enabling a public test before the route changes.","depends_on":["scn_levy_bargain"]},{"id":"scn_public_prediction","title":"A Chart in the Open","summary":"Veya presents the model and its evidence at Mistral Docks, explaining which crossing will shift and when. Kael challenges her, but the predicted wind-current change begins on schedule, forcing him to choose between maintaining his claim and warning the travelers.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Prove the model in time to keep travelers from relying on the threatened crossing.","conflict":"The Cartel's control of shipping gives Kael power to suppress the warning, while Veya risks being wrong in public and Maris fears exposure.","outcome":"The visible shift confirms Veya's prediction; Kael relays the warning rather than conceal it, and travelers begin clearing the threatened route.","depends_on":["scn_claim_stable_route"]},{"id":"scn_route_break","title":"The Crossing Fails","summary":"As the route shifts, Veya directs travelers toward the safer course identified by her model. Maris guides them through the dock's service passages, while Kael relinquishes his hold on the crossing long enough to prevent his toll claim from obstructing their escape.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Get travelers clear of the failing route and demonstrate that the prediction can guide a safer crossing.","conflict":"The route's movement leaves little margin for error, and Kael must act against the monopoly he has been trying to secure.","outcome":"The travelers reach the safer course, the threatened crossing fails, and Veya's chart is publicly vindicated.","depends_on":["scn_public_prediction"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"Shared Bearings","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_open_charts","title":"Charts for the Wardens","summary":"At Silverspine Academy, Veya gives the verified model and its evidence to the Bridge Wardens for use in charting safer routes. She credits Maris's records and invites scrutiny rather than presenting the work as hers alone.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Make the verified prediction useful for maintaining the skybridge network.","conflict":"Veya still wants recognition, but keeping sole control of the charts would repeat the secrecy that endangered others.","outcome":"The Wardens can use the model, and Maris's contribution is recognized without revealing the concealed paths that protect The Hollow.","depends_on":["scn_route_break"]},{"id":"scn_revised_tolls","title":"Terms Beyond the Toll","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael withdraws his claim on the failing crossing and accepts that the routes must be managed using Veya's shared predictions. He agrees to negotiate grain shipments with Maris rather than treating the levy as leverage.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Set new terms for route access and grain shipments after the Cartel's monopoly strategy has been exposed.","conflict":"Kael must give up control he once treated as essential, while Maris has reason to distrust any promise from him.","outcome":"Kael accepts a negotiated arrangement instead of exclusive control, and Maris agrees to discuss supply terms without surrendering her hidden paths.","depends_on":["scn_open_charts"]},{"id":"scn_new_bearings","title":"A Living Map","summary":"Back at Silverspine, Veya and Maris begin a shared record of changing routes, built to be revised as new evidence arrives. Kael's withdrawal of the exclusive claim gives the work room to guide crossings rather than serve a single faction's advantage.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Establish a continuing way to update and share drift predictions.","conflict":"The isles continue to move, and trust between the cartographer, the toll-master, and the miller's daughter remains fragile.","outcome":"The characters commit to adapting the routes together, and Veya accepts that a useful truth must remain open to correction and shared use.","depends_on":["scn_revised_tolls"]}]}]}
</Output>
