{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","title":"The Archipelago Chronicle","logline":"Over a decade of failing winds and breaking skybridges, cartographer Veya must share her charts with the people who can act on them before toll-master Kael seizes the last safe routes and the isles are cut off from one another.","theme":"Knowledge shared can bind a drifting world more surely than control.","acts":[{"id":"act_first_signs","title":"The First Signs","purpose":"setup","scenes":[{"id":"scn_fading_lines","title":"Lines That No Longer Hold","summary":"At Silverspine, Veya compares current bridge observations with her late mentor's records and finds the network shifting faster than the official charts admit.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Verify whether the apparent changes are errors or evidence that the isles are drifting apart.","conflict":"Veya's certainty in her own readings makes her dismiss discrepancies in the old records.","outcome":"Her wind-sight confirms a real shift, but her unfinished chart leaves the safest route uncertain."},{"id":"scn_charter_of_tolls","title":"The Price of Passage","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael proposes raising tolls to fund exclusive control of the routes he believes will remain stable.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael"],"goal":"Secure the Cartel's hold over the most reliable skybridge routes.","conflict":"Kael's belief that price measures worth blinds him to how tolls will burden the isles that depend on shared passage.","outcome":"The Cartel backs his plan, putting Veya's emerging chart and the Wardens in his way."}]},{"id":"act_routes_and_debts","title":"Routes and Debts","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_warning_to_wardens","title":"A Chart Unfinished","summary":"Veya brings the Wardens her evidence and argues that the route toward Emberroost is at risk.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Convince the Wardens to inspect the threatened route before its next crossing season.","conflict":"Because she cannot admit uncertainty, Veya presents a provisional reading as conclusive and loses the Wardens' confidence.","outcome":"The Wardens defer intervention until she can prove the danger, while Veya resolves to test her chart herself.","depends_on":["scn_fading_lines"]},{"id":"scn_maris_resists_levy","title":"The Grain Levy","summary":"At The Hollow, Maris discovers that the Cartel's levy will leave too little grain for her isle and begins using hidden silo paths to protect its stores.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris"],"goal":"Keep enough grain out of the levy to feed The Hollow through the coming season.","conflict":"Her distrust makes her guard the smuggling routes alone, even as Cartel enforcers begin watching the mills.","outcome":"Maris moves a first reserve into concealed storage, but the enforcers' attention makes the route too dangerous to use again.","depends_on":["scn_charter_of_tolls"]}]},{"id":"act_shared_maps","title":"A Map Shared","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_veya_meets_maris","title":"Knowledge for a Passage","summary":"Veya reaches The Hollow with her route notes and offers wind-current knowledge in exchange for Maris's hidden paths.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Find a discreet way to carry Veya's findings to the Wardens and get grain to the people most at risk.","conflict":"Maris fears Veya's chart will expose her routes, while Veya initially refuses to share details she has not fully verified.","outcome":"They agree to exchange only what each needs, forming a cautious alliance and a workable route plan.","depends_on":["scn_warning_to_wardens","scn_maris_resists_levy"]},{"id":"scn_first_shared_crossing","title":"The Crossing's Cost","summary":"Using Veya's current reading and Maris's knowledge of service paths, the pair guides a small grain shipment toward Mistral Docks.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Deliver grain without exposing Maris's remaining stores or losing the crossing route.","conflict":"The route has shifted since Veya mapped it, and the crossing incurs a wind-debt that must be repaid within the season.","outcome":"The shipment arrives, proving the chart useful but imperfect; Veya and Maris accept shared responsibility for repaying the crossing debt.","depends_on":["scn_veya_meets_maris"]}]},{"id":"act_monopoly","title":"The Cartel's Measure","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_kael_claims_routes","title":"A Monopoly of Safe Passage","summary":"Kael moves to claim the last routes he considers stable, arguing at Mistral Docks that exclusive tolls will preserve trade as the bridges fail.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael"],"goal":"Seize control of the remaining dependable skybridge routes before they collapse.","conflict":"His equation of value with price leads him to dismiss the danger that higher tolls will stop grain and forge supplies from moving.","outcome":"The Cartel tightens its hold, and the Wardens accuse Kael of worsening the crisis by restricting access.","depends_on":["scn_first_shared_crossing"]},{"id":"scn_kael_confronts_veya","title":"The Chart He Cannot Buy","summary":"Kael confronts Veya at Silverspine and demands her revised route chart, offering protection in exchange for Cartel control of its use.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Kael seeks Veya's chart; Veya seeks to keep its findings available to the Wardens and the isles.","conflict":"Their former apprenticeship sharpens their rivalry: Kael cannot let Veya's plan succeed, and Veya's refusal to acknowledge gaps in the chart gives him reason to question it.","outcome":"Veya refuses the deal, but Kael learns that her route is still unverified and uses that uncertainty to undermine her credibility.","depends_on":["scn_kael_claims_routes"]}]},{"id":"act_decade_of_drift","title":"Years of Drift","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_season_of_repayment","title":"The Debt Comes Due","summary":"As the route changes over successive seasons, Veya and Maris help the Wardens repay the crossing debt with labor and goods while continuing to update their observations.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Keep the crossing usable without breaking the seasonal wind-debt rule.","conflict":"The bridge's movement makes their old measurements unreliable, and Veya's pride delays accepting Maris's practical corrections.","outcome":"Veya revises the chart with Maris's input; their shared labor keeps the route open for another season and earns the Wardens a more credible warning.","depends_on":["scn_kael_confronts_veya"]},{"id":"scn_grain_route_exposed","title":"A Hidden Path Found","summary":"Cartel enforcers discover signs of Maris's grain route at The Hollow, forcing her to move the reserve before it can be seized.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Maris aims to protect the reserve; Kael seeks to enforce the levy and preserve Cartel control of grain shipments.","conflict":"Maris's slow trust leaves her reluctant to ask Veya for help, while Kael's rigid accounting treats the hidden grain only as lost revenue.","outcome":"Maris moves the reserve in time but loses the route, and Kael's enforcement deepens resistance to the levy.","depends_on":["scn_season_of_repayment"]}]},{"id":"act_broken_route","title":"The Last Stable Bridge","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_route_breaks","title":"The Bridge Gives Way","summary":"At Emberroost, Veya's updated readings warn that the route Kael has claimed is shifting beyond safe use, just as its supplies are needed for repairs.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya seeks to halt unsafe crossings; Kael seeks to keep the route operating under Cartel control.","conflict":"Veya hesitates to publish a reading she cannot guarantee, while Kael interprets the uncertainty as grounds to press ahead.","outcome":"A crossing is stopped before disaster, but the route is effectively lost and the Cartel's remaining claim becomes the center of the crisis.","depends_on":["scn_grain_route_exposed"]},{"id":"scn_wardens_need_evidence","title":"Proof for a Common Plan","summary":"At Silverspine, the Wardens ask Veya to share her raw observations so they can plan repairs across the routes that remain.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Prepare a reliable, shared route plan before the final crossings become unsafe.","conflict":"Veya fears losing control of her work, and Maris worries that exposing her grain paths will invite another levy.","outcome":"Veya shares her records and Maris offers the routes she can safely disclose; the Wardens can now prepare a coordinated response.","depends_on":["scn_route_breaks"]}]},{"id":"act_contest_for_passage","title":"The Contest for Passage","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_kael_seizes_route","title":"The Last Claim","summary":"Kael moves to secure the last stable passage at Mistral Docks, determined to hold the Cartel's monopoly before more routes fail.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael seeks to seize the route; Veya seeks to stop unsafe, exclusive crossings and put the shared chart into use.","conflict":"Kael's fear of losing control makes him reject Veya's evidence, while Veya's old desire for recognition tempts her to insist that her map alone is enough.","outcome":"Veya admits the chart's limits and shows how shared observations make it usable; Kael still refuses to release his claim, forcing the Wardens to act.","depends_on":["scn_wardens_need_evidence"]},{"id":"scn_shared_route_opened","title":"A Route Held in Common","summary":"With the Wardens' repair work guided by Veya's shared chart and Maris's practical paths, the parties meet at Emberroost to decide how the remaining passage can serve all the isles.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Open a safe, common route and end the immediate struggle over exclusive passage.","conflict":"Kael insists that control is the only way to ration scarce crossings, while Maris will not accept another grain levy and Veya refuses to overstate what the chart guarantees.","outcome":"Kael yields exclusive control after recognizing that monopolizing a failing route cannot preserve trade; the Wardens coordinate crossings, and the travelers agree to repay wind-debts through seasonal labor and goods.","depends_on":["scn_kael_seizes_route"]}]},{"id":"act_after_the_claim","title":"What the Wind Leaves","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_new_charting_practice","title":"Many Hands on the Map","summary":"In the seasons after the route agreement, Veya returns to Silverspine to establish a charting practice that records uncertainties and invites reports from other isles.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Make the changing network legible to the people who depend on it.","conflict":"Veya must relinquish the recognition she once sought, and Maris must trust that sharing some knowledge will not expose every hidden path.","outcome":"They publish a shared, revisable chart while keeping sensitive routes guarded, turning their alliance into a lasting practice.","depends_on":["scn_shared_route_opened"]},{"id":"scn_trade_without_monopoly","title":"The Cost of Control","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael works within the new crossing arrangement as the Cartel's tolls give way to agreed seasonal contributions.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael aims to keep trade moving without reclaiming exclusive control; Veya seeks to ensure the shared chart remains in use.","conflict":"Kael must accept that worth cannot be reduced to price, while Veya must trust the agreement without pretending it can stop the islands from drifting.","outcome":"They maintain a wary cooperation: the routes still change, but the isles now share the knowledge and work needed to adapt.","depends_on":["scn_new_charting_practice"]}]}]}
