ms_routes"]}]},{"id":"act_decade_of_drift","title":"Years of Drift","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_season_of_repayment","title":"The Debt Comes Due","summary":"As the route changes over successive seasons, Veya and Maris help the Wardens repay the crossing debt with labor and goods while continuing to update their observations.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Keep the crossing usable without breaking the seasonal wind-debt rule.","conflict":"The bridge's movement makes their old measurements unreliable, and Veya's pride delays accepting Maris's practical corrections.","outcome":"Veya revises the chart with Maris's input; their shared labor keeps the route open for another season and earns the Wardens a more credible warning.","depends_on":["scn_kael_confronts_veya"]},{"id":"scn_grain_route_exposed","title":"A Hidden Path Found","summary":"Cartel enforcers discover signs of Maris's grain route at The Hollow, forcing her to move the reserve before it can be seized.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Maris aims to protect the reserve; Kael seeks to enforce the levy and preserve Cartel control of grain shipments.","conflict":"Maris's slow trust leaves her reluctant to ask Veya for help, while Kael's rigid accounting treats the hidden grain only as lost revenue.","outcome":"Maris moves the reserve in time but loses the route, and Kael's enforcement deepens resistance to the levy.","depends_on":["scn_season_of_repayment"]}]},{"id":"act_broken_route","title":"The Last Stable Bridge","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_route_breaks","title":"The Bridge Gives Way","summary":"At Emberroost, Veya's updated readings warn that the route Kael has claimed is shifting beyond safe use, just as its supplies are needed for repairs.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya seeks to halt unsafe crossings; Kael seeks to keep the route operating under Cartel control.","conflict":"Veya hesitates to publish a reading she cannot guarantee, while Kael interprets the uncertainty as grounds to press ahead.","outcome":"A crossing is stopped before disaster, but the route is effectively lost and the Cartel's remaining claim becomes the center of the crisis.","depends_on":["scn_grain_route_exposed"]},{"id":"scn_wardens_need_evidence","title":"Proof for a Common Plan","summary":"At Silverspine, the Wardens ask Veya to share her raw observations so they can plan repairs across the routes that remain.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Prepare a reliable, shared route plan before the final crossings become unsafe.","conflict":"Veya fears losing control of her work, and Maris worries that exposing her grain paths will invite another levy.","outcome":"Veya shares her records and Maris offers the routes she can safely disclose; the Wardens can now prepare a coordinated response.","depends_on":["scn_route_breaks"]}]},{"id":"act_contest_for_passage","title":"The Contest for Passage","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_kael_seizes_route","title":"The Last Claim","summary":"Kael moves to secure the last stable passage at Mistral Docks, determined to hold the Cartel's monopoly before more routes fail.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael seeks to seize the route; Veya seeks to stop unsafe, exclusive crossings and put the shared chart into use.","conflict":"Kael's fear of losing control makes him reject Veya's evidence, while Veya's old desire for recognition tempts her to insist that her map alone is enough.","outcome":"Veya admits the chart's limits and shows how shared observations make it usable; Kael still refuses to release his claim, forcing the Wardens to act.","depends_on":["scn_wardens_need_evidence"]},{"id":"scn_shared_route_opened","title":"A Route Held in Common","summary":"With the Wardens' repair work guided by Veya's shared chart and Maris's practical paths, the parties meet at Emberroost to decide how the remaining passage can serve all the isles.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Open a safe, common route and end the immediate struggle over exclusive passage.","conflict":"Kael insists that control is the only way to ration scarce crossings, while Maris will not accept another grain levy and Veya refuses to overstate what the chart guarantees.","outcome":"Kael yields exclusive control after recognizing that monopolizing a failing route cannot preserve trade; the Wardens coordinate crossings, and the travelers agree to repay wind-debts through seasonal labor and goods.","depends_on":["scn_kael_seizes_route"]}]},{"id":"act_after_the_claim","title":"What the Wind Leaves","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_new_charting_practice","title":"Many Hands on the Map","summary":"In the seasons after the route agreement, Veya returns to Silverspine to establish a charting practice that records uncertainties and invites reports from other isles.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Make the changing network legible to the people who depend on it.","conflict":"Veya must relinquish the recognition she once sought, and Maris must trust that sharing some knowledge will not expose every hidden path.","outcome":"They publish a shared, revisable chart while keeping sensitive routes guarded, turning their alliance into a lasting practice.","depends_on":["scn_shared_route_opened"]},{"id":"scn_trade_without_monopoly","title":"The Cost of Control","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael works within the new crossing arrangement as the Cartel's tolls give way to agreed seasonal contributions.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael aims to keep trade moving without reclaiming exclusive control; Veya seeks to ensure the shared