 the route operating under Cartel control.","conflict":"Veya hesitates to publish a reading she cannot guarantee, while Kael interprets the uncertainty as grounds to press ahead.","outcome":"A crossing is stopped before disaster, but the route is effectively lost and the Cartel's remaining claim becomes the center of the crisis.","depends_on":["scn_grain_route_exposed"]},{"id":"scn_wardens_need_evidence","title":"Proof for a Common Plan","summary":"At Silverspine, the Wardens ask Veya to share her raw observations so they can plan repairs across the routes that remain.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Prepare a reliable, shared route plan before the final crossings become unsafe.","conflict":"Veya fears losing control of her work, and Maris worries that exposing her grain paths will invite another levy.","outcome":"Veya shares her records and Maris offers the routes she can safely disclose; the Wardens can now prepare a coordinated response.","depends_on":["scn_route_breaks"]}]},{"id":"act_contest_for_passage","title":"The Contest for Passage","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_kael_seizes_route","title":"The Last Claim","summary":"Kael moves to secure the last stable passage at Mistral Docks, determined to hold the Cartel's monopoly before more routes fail.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael seeks to seize the route; Veya seeks to stop unsafe, exclusive crossings and put the shared chart into use.","conflict":"Kael's fear of losing control makes him reject Veya's evidence, while Veya's old desire for recognition tempts her to insist that her map alone is enough.","outcome":"Veya admits the chart's limits and shows how shared observations make it usable; Kael still refuses to release his claim, forcing the Wardens to act.","depends_on":["scn_wardens_need_evidence"]},{"id":"scn_shared_route_opened","title":"A Route Held in Common","summary":"With the Wardens' repair work guided by Veya's shared chart and Maris's practical paths, the parties meet at Emberroost to decide how the remaining passage can serve all the isles.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Open a safe, common route and end the immediate struggle over exclusive passage.","conflict":"Kael insists that control is the only way to ration scarce crossings, while Maris will not accept another grain levy and Veya refuses to overstate what the chart guarantees.","outcome":"Kael yields exclusive control after recognizing that monopolizing a failing route cannot preserve trade; the Wardens coordinate crossings, and the travelers agree to repay wind-debts through seasonal labor and goods.","depends_on":["scn_kael_seizes_route"]}]},{"id":"act_after_the_claim","title":"What the Wind Leaves","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_new_charting_practice","title":"Many Hands on the Map","summary":"In the seasons after the route agreement, Veya returns to Silverspine to establish a charting practice that records uncertainties and invites reports from other isles.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Make the changing network legible to the people who depend on it.","conflict":"Veya must relinquish the recognition she once sought, and Maris must trust that sharing some knowledge will not expose every hidden path.","outcome":"They publish a shared, revisable chart while keeping sensitive routes guarded, turning their alliance into a lasting practice.","depends_on":["scn_shared_route_opened"]},{"id":"scn_trade_without_monopoly","title":"The Cost of Control","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael works within the new crossing arrangement as the Cartel's tolls give way to agreed seasonal contributions.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael aims to keep trade moving without reclaiming exclusive control; Veya seeks to ensure the shared chart remains in use.","conflict":"Kael must accept that worth cannot be reduced to price, while Veya must trust the agreement without pretending it can stop the islands from drifting.","outcome":"They maintain a wary cooperation: the routes still change, but the isles now share the knowledge and work needed to adapt.","depends_on":["scn_new_charting_practice"]}]}]}
